From: BiliHarmony maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ohcodec: tolerate failed interop initialization during cleanup

ra_hwdec loading calls uninit() even when init() failed. An unsupported
GL/Vulkan interop leaves p->interop unset, so cleanup must not dereference it.
Successful initialization follows the existing owner_uninit path unchanged.

diff --git a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c
--- a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c
+++ b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_ohcodec.c
@@ -147,7 +147,8 @@
     hwdec_devices_remove(hw->devs, &p->hwctx);
     // Decoder and device disappear before listener/NativeImage/GPU objects.
     av_buffer_unref(&p->hwctx.av_device_ref);
-    p->interop->owner_uninit(hw);
+    if (p->interop)
+        p->interop->owner_uninit(hw);
 }
 
 static int mapper_init(struct ra_hwdec_mapper *mapper)
